{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 cb pump\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A tempo-synced volume shaper: the house and EDM "pump" without sidechain routing. The gain reaches its minimum exactly on each period start (the beat, at 1/4) and recovers over the release share of the period. Zero latency, stereo-linked, and unity while the transport is stopped.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Rate}: 1/16T to 1 bar, with dotted and triplet values.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Depth}: how far the gain dips; 0 % leaves the signal bit for bit unchanged.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Shape}: Duck, Linear, Exponential or Gate.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Release}: the share of the period the gain takes to come back.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Phase offset}: moves the dip within the period.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Trigger}: tempo sync, or one dip per MIDI note-on. MIDI passes through.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
